00:10:11.520 --> 00:10:13.680
and it really was smooth and easy,

00:10:13.680 --> 00:10:16.130
and I sleep better at night
knowing that I have a policy.

00:10:16.130 --> 00:10:18.470
So thank you Policy Genius
for sponsoring this video,

00:10:18.470 --> 00:10:20.170
for supporting my work and my channel.

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:21.550
That link will be in my description.

00:10:21.550 --> 00:10:24.010
Now let's get back to the Panama Canal.

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:26.770
So Philippe is now the
ambassador of the Panamanians,

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:28.260
who are not a country yet,

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.270
but he's still hoping
that maybe the Colombians

00:10:30.270 --> 00:10:31.600
will approve the plan.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:33.850
Philippe sort of has
this in his back pocket,

00:10:33.850 --> 00:10:36.370
this deal that he just
made with the Panamanians.

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:38.060
He doesn't know if he has to use it yet.

00:10:38.060 --> 00:10:39.410
But back to the Americans

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:42.570
having to ask Colombia for
approval to build their canal.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:44.707
Sure enough, they show
up and Colombia's like,

00:10:44.707 --> 00:10:46.497
"No, go home.

00:10:46.497 --> 00:10:48.647
"You guys are way too
aggressive around here lately.

00:10:48.647 --> 00:10:49.697
"We're not interested.

00:10:49.697 --> 00:10:51.250
"No canal, see you later."

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:53.077
So the US goes to Philippe and they say,

00:10:53.077 --> 00:10:54.647
"Sorry bro, the deal is off.

00:10:54.647 --> 00:10:55.857
"Colombia said no.

00:10:55.857 --> 00:10:58.357
"We said we'd only do
this if Colombia said yes.

00:10:58.357 --> 00:11:00.610
"After all, Panama is a part of Colombia."

00:11:00.610 --> 00:11:02.847
And Philippe is like, "Wait, hold on.

00:11:02.847 --> 00:11:04.017
"I have a plan for this.

00:11:04.017 --> 00:11:05.897
"I've been talking to the Panamanians

00:11:05.897 --> 00:11:08.267
"and they want to break
away from Colombia,

00:11:08.267 --> 00:11:10.437
"and they made me their ambassador.

00:11:10.437 --> 00:11:12.077
"I've even written them a new Constitution

00:11:12.077 --> 00:11:14.000
"and designed them a new flag."

00:11:14.000 --> 00:11:15.667
Wait, Philippe, are
you a graphic designer?

00:11:15.667 --> 00:11:17.967
"No, but I designed them a flag anyway.

00:11:17.967 --> 00:11:20.667
"We can still make this
canal thing happen.

00:11:20.667 --> 00:11:23.547
"All I need you guys to do
is show up with your navy

00:11:23.547 --> 00:11:25.097
"to make sure that the Panamanians

00:11:25.097 --> 00:11:26.717
"can rise up for independence

00:11:26.717 --> 00:11:29.280
"without Colombia coming
to shut it all down."

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:30.317
And the US Congress is like,

00:11:30.317 --> 00:11:32.350
"Dude, you're nuts, see you later."

00:11:32.350 --> 00:11:36.050
But out of nowhere, the
President at the time shows up

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:39.457
and is like, "Did somebody say
stage a theatrical revolution

00:11:39.457 --> 00:11:42.260
"to take over more land and
increase American power?"

00:11:42.260 --> 00:11:43.820
Teddy was back on the scene.

00:11:43.820 --> 00:11:45.230
Teddy loves this kind of stuff.

00:11:45.230 --> 00:11:48.067
He loves the sort of backroom deals,

00:11:48.067 --> 00:11:51.770
"Let's not ask for permission,
let's ask for forgiveness."

00:11:51.770 --> 00:11:54.310
This is Teddy Roosevelt's sweet spot.

00:11:54.310 --> 00:11:56.190
So Philippe has all of his ducks in a row.

00:11:56.190 --> 00:11:58.050
He's got Teddy Roosevelt on his side,

00:11:58.050 --> 00:12:00.030
he has Panamanians who
just gave him approval

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:01.470
to be their ambassador,

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:03.050
and he's like, "Let's do this."

00:12:03.050 --> 00:12:06.290
So in November 1903,
Philippe gives the nod

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:08.030
to the Panamanians to rise up,

00:12:08.030 --> 00:12:10.250
to take over and declare
themselves independent.

00:12:10.250 --> 00:12:12.970
And at the same time, he
signals to Teddy Roosevelt

00:12:12.970 --> 00:12:15.300
to send in their big gun boats

00:12:15.300 --> 00:12:17.120
to sit off the coast of Panama

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:19.830
to block Colombia from
sending in reinforcements

00:12:19.830 --> 00:12:22.370
to put down this revolution
by the Panamanians.

00:12:22.370 --> 00:12:25.367
And so Colombia is
like, "Oh fine, take it.

00:12:25.367 --> 00:12:26.587
"F you, America.

00:12:26.587 --> 00:12:28.577
"You guys played real dirty there, okay?

00:12:28.577 --> 00:12:29.417
"You know that?

00:12:29.417 --> 00:12:30.540
"That was not cool."

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:32.640
So just as Philippe orchestrated,

00:12:32.640 --> 00:12:34.940
Panama declares independence,

00:12:34.940 --> 00:12:36.760
and Philippe is the ambassador.

00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:40.150
The US is the first to
recognize them as a new country,

00:12:40.150 --> 00:12:42.787
and Teddy Roosevelt's
like, "That was thrilling!

00:12:42.787 --> 00:12:44.070
"Now what, Philippe?"

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:46.407
So Philippe is like, "Let's
make a deal, America.

00:12:46.407 --> 00:12:49.047
"I'm the official
representative of Panama now,

00:12:49.047 --> 00:12:51.097
"as per my agreement with the Panamanians,

00:12:51.097 --> 00:12:53.990
"so let's write a treaty
on behalf of Panama."

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:55.340
So he travels to the United States

00:12:55.340 --> 00:12:56.550
and starts working on a treaty

00:12:56.550 --> 00:12:58.320
between the United States and Panama

00:12:58.320 --> 00:13:01.410
that would give the USA
the rights and sovereignty

00:13:01.410 --> 00:13:04.140
over this strip of land to build a canal.

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:06.130
I mean, this series of events is insane.

00:13:06.130 --> 00:13:07.760
France fails to build a canal,

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:10.060
so one French dude, an engineer,

00:13:10.060 --> 00:13:11.610
tries to redeem the whole thing

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:15.330
by convincing the US to change
the location of their canal,

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:16.830
and then creates a revolution

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:20.010
and convinces the US to
help back that revolution,

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:22.830
so that he, a Frenchman,
can be the ambassador

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:25.060
of the newly created country of Panama,

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:28.040
and make a deal with the US.

00:13:28.040 --> 00:13:29.450
Whoa, Philippe.

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:31.980
He was the one man band lobbyist

00:13:31.980 --> 00:13:35.050
who somehow finagled this whole situation.

00:13:35.050 --> 00:13:37.430
So Philippe and the Secretary
of State of the United States

00:13:37.430 --> 00:13:39.740
draw up this treaty that
gives the US total control

00:13:39.740 --> 00:13:42.310
over this strip of land for
them to build their canal.

00:13:42.310 --> 00:13:44.380
No Panamanians were in the room

00:13:44.380 --> 00:13:45.740
when they drafted this treaty.

00:13:45.740 --> 00:13:47.770
They gave no approval of this.

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:50.150
This treaty was between the US and Panama,

00:13:50.150 --> 00:13:51.980
but really it was between the US

00:13:51.980 --> 00:13:54.230
and Philippe the French engineer.

00:13:54.230 --> 00:13:56.440
So now the US military shows up to Panama

00:13:56.440 --> 00:13:59.370
to claim this land that
they now see as theirs,

00:13:59.370 --> 00:14:00.507
and the Panamanians are like,

00:14:00.507 --> 00:14:02.640
"Dude, WTF, what are you doing here?"

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:05.237
And the US is like, "Oh,
you signed a treaty with us

00:14:05.237 --> 00:14:06.590
"giving us all this land."

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:08.350
And Panama's like, "No we didn't."

00:14:08.350 --> 00:14:10.577
And then they're like,
"Oh wait, light bulb.

00:14:10.577 --> 00:14:11.647
"Philippe!

00:14:11.647 --> 00:14:14.037
"That's why he wanted
to be our ambassador!

00:14:14.037 --> 00:14:14.870
"I get it.

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.600
"Man, we got played by Philippe."

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:17.570
And they totally did.

00:14:17.570 --> 00:14:20.670
So now the US is setting up shop in Panama

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:22.625
to start digging their canal.

00:14:22.625 --> 00:14:25.708
(film strip rolling)

00:14:28.640 --> 00:14:31.410
The US picked up right
where the French left off,

00:14:31.410 --> 00:14:34.010
using effectively the same
route that the French had dug

00:14:34.010 --> 00:14:35.640
during their seven years of misery.

00:14:35.640 --> 00:14:38.570
And speaking of misery,
the US was able to learn

00:14:38.570 --> 00:14:39.990
from the French's mistakes.

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:42.480
They started using railways
to truck out all the dirt,

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.090
so that the mud wouldn't
slide back into the canal,

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:47.680
and they learned how to
drain the puddles of water

00:14:47.680 --> 00:14:52.320
so that it wasn't a haven for
disease infected mosquitoes.

00:14:52.320 --> 00:14:55.580
And most importantly, they
didn't try the crackpot idea

00:14:55.580 --> 00:14:58.700
of trying to dig a canal all
the way down to sea level.

00:14:58.700 --> 00:15:00.230
They went with the much better idea

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:04.730
of digging the canal up high,
26 meters above sea level,

00:15:04.730 --> 00:15:07.657
and using clever engineering
to get ships up to that level.

00:15:07.657 --> 00:15:10.430
"Like I said", said that
one French engineer,

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:11.397
and de Lesseps was like,

00:15:11.397 --> 00:15:13.050
"No one asked you, get out of here."

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:14.540
So after 10 years of construction

00:15:14.540 --> 00:15:16.140
and a visit by Teddy Roosevelt,

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:18.040
who staged this amazing photo shoot

00:15:18.040 --> 00:15:20.190
of him wearing a Panamanian hat,

00:15:20.190 --> 00:15:21.719
sitting on one of the machines,

00:15:21.719 --> 00:15:24.360
all to boost morale to
get this project done,

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:27.450
after all of that, the
US completed this dream

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:29.060
of slicing a water route

00:15:29.060 --> 00:15:31.350
through this 80 kilometer stretch of land.

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:33.740
Philippe, at this point,
is back in France,

00:15:33.740 --> 00:15:36.600
probably exhausted from
all of his scheming,

00:15:36.600 --> 00:15:39.580
but ultimately very pleased
that he was able to pull it off.

00:15:39.580 --> 00:15:42.296
So the canal is done,
and here's how it works.

00:15:42.296 --> 00:15:44.890
(water rushing)

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:46.960
Remember that the land looks like this.

00:15:46.960 --> 00:15:50.030
You have the Pacific and Atlantic
Oceans here at sea level,

00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:51.540
and then the interior of the land

00:15:51.540 --> 00:15:54.210
being about 26 meters above sea level.

00:15:54.210 --> 00:15:56.220
So first, they built a dam on this river

00:15:56.220 --> 00:15:58.040
to create this giant lake,

00:15:58.040 --> 00:16:00.310
so that they have loads
of water to work with.

00:16:00.310 --> 00:16:03.650
That's why we see those trees
sticking up from the water,

00:16:03.650 --> 00:16:06.020
or why these hilltops turned into islands.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:09.210
Then they built these brilliant
inventions called locks.

00:16:09.210 --> 00:16:11.530
The boat enters here at sea level.

00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:14.450
They enter into this chamber
where there is a gate

00:16:14.450 --> 00:16:17.970
that is holding the water
from the high up lake back.

00:16:17.970 --> 00:16:18.810
It's locked.

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:20.610
But once the boat is in
this holding chamber,

00:16:20.610 --> 00:16:23.120
they let the water from
higher up come down,

00:16:23.120 --> 00:16:24.950
making the boat flow up.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:27.860
It takes about eight minutes
for the boat to rise.

00:16:27.860 --> 00:16:29.610
Then they move into the next chamber,

00:16:29.610 --> 00:16:32.090
where they do this again and again,

00:16:32.090 --> 00:16:34.500
until by the end of it,
the boat has been lifted up

00:16:34.500 --> 00:16:36.540
26 meters above sea level.

00:16:36.540 --> 00:16:38.810
They then traverse the rest of this canal,

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:41.280
going through the artificial
lake and snaking through

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:42.660
until they get to the other side,

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:45.330
where now they need to
get down to sea level.

00:16:45.330 --> 00:16:47.810
And they go through the same
process, but in reverse.

00:16:47.810 --> 00:16:49.180
They finally make it down to sea level

00:16:49.180 --> 00:16:52.380
and they can exit onto
now a different ocean

00:16:52.380 --> 00:16:53.530
than when they started.

00:16:55.860 --> 00:16:57.790
It's honestly an engineering marvel,

00:16:57.790 --> 00:17:00.560
and it reshaped the
global economic landscape,

00:17:00.560 --> 00:17:04.010
making it easier and safer
to move goods and people

00:17:04.010 --> 00:17:04.980
around the world.

00:17:04.980 --> 00:17:08.060
And yeah, the US was very
serious about controlling

00:17:08.060 --> 00:17:09.340
this little strip of land,

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:11.150
this choke point that they had built.

00:17:11.150 --> 00:17:14.860
If you look at a map from
the early or mid 1900s,

00:17:14.860 --> 00:17:16.830
you're gonna see that
the Panama Canal zone

00:17:16.830 --> 00:17:19.880
was always marked as a
sovereign part of the US.

00:17:19.880 --> 00:17:21.710
Controlling a choke point like this

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:25.217
gives you strong strategic
advantage, and the US knew that.

00:17:25.217 --> 00:17:28.540
But the world would finally
decide that big powers

00:17:28.540 --> 00:17:30.850
shouldn't actually be able to swoop in

00:17:30.850 --> 00:17:33.173
and take over whatever land they want.

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:37.990
- [Newscaster] The wind of
change is blowing up a gale

00:17:37.990 --> 00:17:39.850
in the Panama Canal zone,

00:17:39.850 --> 00:17:41.530
and citizens have to defend themselves

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:44.110
as students and other
rioters demanded the names

00:17:44.110 --> 00:17:47.207
of the 61 year old Canal Zone
Treaty with the United States.

00:17:47.207 --> 00:17:50.740
- And the Panamanians in the
1960s finally had enough,

00:17:50.740 --> 00:17:53.580
and they're like, "Yeah,
this land is actually ours."

00:17:53.580 --> 00:17:56.720
So in the 60s and 70s, the
Panamanians rose up in protest

00:17:56.720 --> 00:17:58.680
against this US occupation of the canal,

00:17:58.680 --> 00:18:01.600
and through a series of treaties,
they finally got it back.

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:04.270
Officially on the last
day of the millennium,

00:18:04.270 --> 00:18:07.660
December 31, 1999, they
signed the last treaty

00:18:07.660 --> 00:18:09.640
that returned sovereignty to Panama.

00:18:09.640 --> 00:18:13.089
And then Jimmy Carter
gave a speech in Spanish.

00:18:13.089 --> 00:18:17.150
(Jimmy Carter speaking Spanish)

00:18:17.150 --> 00:18:21.390
I mean, he, he tried really
hard, and I guess that matters.

00:18:21.390 --> 00:18:24.360
So today, the Panama Canal
belongs to Panamanians.

00:18:24.360 --> 00:18:27.730
It still uses the innovative
technology from 100 years ago

00:18:27.730 --> 00:18:29.690
that allows this canal to be built

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:31.650
26 meters above sea level.

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:33.710
But for all of the engineering innovation

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:34.690
that's present here,

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:37.110
to me, the more incredible
part of this story

00:18:37.110 --> 00:18:40.390
is how this one Frenchman
orchestrated all of this.

00:18:40.390 --> 00:18:42.410
He played all the geopolitical forces

00:18:42.410 --> 00:18:44.080
at the time just right.

00:18:44.080 --> 00:18:46.760
He used Panamanians'
thirst for independence

00:18:46.760 --> 00:18:50.140
and the Americans' thirst for
imperialism and ocean power,

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:53.410
all to make his dream
of this canal happen.

00:18:53.410 --> 00:18:56.240
Oh, and to secure his financial
return on the project.

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:58.160
What a wild story.

00:18:58.160 --> 00:18:59.160
Thanks for watching.

00:19:00.089 --> 00:19:02.589
(light music)

